            <ArticleTitle>Recent research on inhaled corticosteroids and growth.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>53-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/MED.0b013e32834edab5</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="PURPOSE OF REVIEW" NlmCategory="OBJECTIVE">Description of recent studies evaluating growth and inhaled corticosteroids.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="RECENT FINDINGS" NlmCategory="RESULTS">Corticosteroids are the gold standard of asthma maintenance treatment, but effects on growth remain controversial. This is a review of recent research in this area, which has focused on medications causing less adrenal suppression as well as alternative regimens for chronic illness such as asthma.</AbstractText>
                <AbstractText Label="SUMMARY" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">The use of newer corticosteroids and regimens shows short-term evidence of minimal growth effects without worsening of asthma control.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
